---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Experience — Mohammed Fawaz">
  <h1 class="section-title">EXPERIENCE</h1>

  <div class="exp-header">
    <span class="exp-role">Research & Development Intern — Robotics</span>
    <span class="exp-org">AIRAT Systems LLP</span>
    <span class="exp-period">5 January 2026 – 30 April 2026 · 16 weeks</span>
  </div>

  <p class="exp-intro">
    Joined as an R&D intern at AIRAT Systems, an AI/Robotics/Automation firm working across
    healthcare, agriculture, and consumer technology verticals. Owned two full projects end-to-end,
    from literature review and CAD through fabrication, software integration, and validation.
  </p>

  <section class="phase">
    <h2>Phase 1 — Humanoid Desktop Animatronic Robot (Weeks 1–8)</h2>
    <p>
      Started by auditing the existing prototype — a Raspberry Pi 4-based desktop companion robot
      with visible mechanical instability and no headroom for real-time AI inference. Spent the
      first week on literature review (servo-driven facial expression systems, PCA9685 control,
      embedded AI platforms) and produced a formal gap analysis across structural, computational,
      and software dimensions before writing a design brief for guide sign-off.
    </p>
    <p>
      Redesigned the full mechanical shell in Fusion 360 — internal ribs for rigidity, reinforced
      servo mounting zones, a dedicated low-CG compartment for the new compute board, ventilation
      slots for thermal management, and internal cable channels. Migrated the compute platform from
      Raspberry Pi 4 to an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super for CUDA-accelerated on-device inference,
      then rebuilt the control software as a multithreaded Python architecture running face
      tracking, speech-to-text, and servo actuation in parallel. Integrated the Groq API directly
      for agentic tool-calling, bypassing heavier frameworks, which brought conversational latency
      down to roughly 1.3 seconds.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="phase">
    <h2>Phase 2 — ArecaSort V1: AI-Driven Arecanut Sorting (Weeks 9–16)</h2>
    <p>
      Second project addressed a real agricultural bottleneck — arecanut grading was slow,
      inconsistent, manual work. Began with market research into grading standards, then designed
      the full machine in Fusion 360: feed hopper, conveyor, camera station, and a pneumatic sorting
      mechanism using solenoid valves for millisecond-precision gate actuation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Personally sourced physical arecanut samples across all four quality grades from a local
      agricultural market, then built and ran a controlled photography rig (diffuse LED lighting,
      fixed camera position, neutral background) to capture a consistent labelled dataset. Trained
      and evaluated six architectures — YOLOv8, YOLOv10, EfficientDet, MobileNet-SSD V2, ResNet-50,
      and a custom CNN — before selecting YOLOv10 with TensorRT FP16 quantization for deployment.
      Final system reached ~91% sorting accuracy at 45 units/minute, validated with additional
      lighting-robustness testing before handover.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .section-title { font-family: var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .exp-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .exp-role { font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--line-bright); }
  .exp-org { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .exp-period { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--line); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .exp-intro { line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem; color: var(--line-bright); }
  .phase {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .phase h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .phase p { line-height: 1.7; color: var(--line-bright); }
</style>